===== sruman provide-umu --help
Make a runtime umu's folder under `$XDG_DATA_HOME/sruman/umu/`, so umu runs it instead of downloading its own

Usage: sruman provide-umu [OPTIONS] <RUNTIME|--appid <ID>>

Arguments:
  [RUNTIME]
          The runtime, optionally `=build`; the current build by default

Options:
      --appid <ID>
          Pick the runtime by Steam app id (Proton's `require_tool_appid`)

  -y, --yes
          Answer every prompt with its default

      --color <WHEN>
          Colorize the output
          
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

  -q, --quiet
          Less output (`runtimes`: names only)

  -v, --verbose...
          Log to stderr (-vv: more)

      --config <FILE>
          Use this config.toml

